  "notes": "Authored for due2: the three nested cases reported to OVAL on DIPS-Tools/ODRL-Engine#9 (2026-10-19), and a fourth under negation. No origin result: the vendored OVAL suite (40b8ac6) predates them. OVAL at 596f10c, given the same values in the request, accepts scenario 1 as a full match, because its first pass reads the missing resolution as false. It asks for `media eq Poster or system eq PC` in scenario 2, where only `system eq PC` can help, and for `media eq Poster and system eq PC` in scenario 3, where `system eq PC` is enough. due2 answers Indeterminate in all four. It names the unknown parts of every atom that is not F (workflows §3.5), so scenarios 2 and 4 do not name media, which lies only in an F atom, and scenario 3 names media, which decides nothing. Scenario 1 is due2-xone-unknown's first trap with three members.",
